# Planted bugs for the gte-with-dedup design. Each one must make its
# property fail.
run fv-tlc WatermarkCursor.tla GteWithDedup.cfg WitnessSlowCommit.cfg
properties ExactlyOnce EventuallyBothRan
file WatermarkCursor.tla

mutation the query drops back to a strict comparison against the cursor
detects ExactlyOnce
- Matches(r) == IF UsesGte THEN CT[r] >= cursor ELSE CT[r] > cursor
+ Matches(r) == CT[r] > cursor

mutation the second run stays possible but nothing ever requires it to happen
detects EventuallyBothRan
- Work == CommitLate \/ Run1 \/ Run2
- Next == Work \/ Done
+ Work == CommitLate \/ Run1
+ Next == Work \/ Run2 \/ Done

harmless a comment on the dedup set
- \* Source: loader.run(), one pass of the incremental query and cursor move.
+ \* Source: loader.run(). One pass of the incremental query and cursor move.
